# Automation Standards

## Naming convention

- Test title: `<TestCaseId> | <Module> - <Short scenario>` (regex prefix: `/^[A-Z]+-\d+\s*\|/`).
- Spec files: `tests/<module>/<feature>.spec.ts`.
- Page objects: `pages/<module>/<Name>Page.ts` extending `BasePage` where practical.

## Folder structure (each new module)

1. Add URL fragment → `test-data/module-urls.ts`.
2. Add Page Object → `pages/<module>/`.
3. Add spec → `tests/<module>/`.
4. Register coverage in `docs/test_cases.md` (canonical path; Linux CI is case-sensitive).

## Selector priority (Scriptcase)

1. `getByRole` with accessible name.
2. `getByLabel` / `getByPlaceholder`.
3. `locator('[name="..."]')`.
4. `getByText` / `filter({ hasText })`.
5. Never: dynamic `id` with hash suffix, brittle absolute XPath.

## POM method style

- Methods expose business language, not raw selectors.
- Iframe resolution for Scriptcase shell: use `BasePage.content()` / `grid()`; dashboard widgets use helpers in `utils/frame-helper.ts` (see below).

## Dashboard two-view architecture

The dashboard uses separate widget iframes (`dbifrm_widget*`). Use the matching page object and frame helpers:

**Cultural Dashboard view (default on load)**

- `widget8` — Cultural Activities (`frameCulturalActivities`).
- `widget9` — Procedure Misses (`frameProcedureMisses`).
- `widget10` — controls: `#year-select`, "User Dashboard" (`frameControls` / `controlsFrame()`).
- `CulturalDashboardPage.yearDropdown()` → `#year-select` inside **widget10**.

**User Dashboard view (after "User Dashboard" in widget10)**

- `widget6` — nav: `#year-select`, "Cultural Dashboard" (`frameDashboardNav` / `dashboardNavFrame()`).
- `widget7` — Leave Summary (`frameLeaveSummary`).
- `UserDashboardPage.yearDropdown()` → `#year-select` inside **widget6**.

**Rules**

- Do not assert Cultural panels (`widget8`/`widget9`) from tests that only opened the User Dashboard view.
- Do not use `UserDashboardPage.yearDropdown()` semantics for Cultural-only specs; `CulturalDashboardPage` overrides `yearDropdown()` for widget10.
- `CulturalDashboardPage.openDashboard()` must not click "User Dashboard".
- `UserDashboardPage.openDashboard()` should switch to User view when the Cultural controls frame shows "User Dashboard".

## Docs alignment

- Every automated case should appear in `docs/test_cases.md`.
- Blocked/skipped tests: include a reason in `test.skip()` / `test.fail()`.
